# Paths staged into the release tarball, repo-relative.
#
# ENUMERATED, never the bare `grand-rounds/` directory. make-federation-bundle
# uses `cp -pR`, which does not honour .gitignore, so a directory line packages
# whatever the operator's working tree happens to contain — a locally built
# tarball shipped baseline/.agentis/ (an Ed25519 private key), a real
# config/colony.toml, and gated work/*.vcf, with every bundle test still green.
# Official releases build from a fresh CI checkout and were unaffected, but a
# manifest must not depend on that. dark-factory and tribes-bench enumerate for
# the same reason.
grand-rounds/README.md
grand-rounds/CHANGELOG.md
grand-rounds/LICENSE
grand-rounds/VERSION
grand-rounds/install.sh
grand-rounds/.gitignore
grand-rounds/doc/
grand-rounds/tools/
grand-rounds/baseline/README.md
grand-rounds/baseline/demo-baseline.sh
grand-rounds/baseline/demo-baseline-live.sh
grand-rounds/baseline/demo-lens-smoke-real.sh
grand-rounds/baseline/agents/
grand-rounds/baseline/config/
grand-rounds/baseline/fixtures/
grand-rounds/baseline/scripts/
grand-rounds/baseline/settings/

# demo-baseline.sh mutation-tests the leak guard against a throwaway git tree,
# so the guard must ship. Its repo-scoped tree scan skips in a bundle, which has
# no .git — see demo-baseline.sh.
tools/check-no-gated-data.sh
